                <pb facs="0462" n="1422" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1422"/>

                <head>No. 966.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 21, of March 30 last, on the
                    subject of Frary and Arteaga gives satisfaction to the Department, which,
                    however, awaits further information as to the former case.</p>
                <p>Should it be necessary, fresh instructions will be sent in regard to that of
                    Arteaga.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
